{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>The entire commandment.</b> According to its plain sense. And its midrash aggadah: if you have begun a commandment, finish it — for it is called only after the one who completes it, as it says, ״וְאֶת עַצְמוֹת יוֹסֵף אֲשֶׁר הֶעֱלוּ בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל מִמִּצְרַיִם קָבְרוּ בִּשְׁכֶם״ (Joshua 24) — but was it not Moses alone who occupied himself with bringing them up? Rather, because he did not live to complete it and Israel completed it, it is called by their name (Tanchuma)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:20.165393007Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}